# Graphics Card listing + PDP required info

Every Graphics Card (category slugs `graphics-card`, `nvidia`, `amd-gpu`) must expose structured specs and show them on the **listing card** and **PDP**. Do not ship a GPU card that is only a title + price.

## Required structured specs

Store these as `productSpecification` keys (not only HTML in `description`):

| Key | Listing card | PDP |
|-----|--------------|-----|
| `memory_size` | Video Memory | yes |
| `memory_type` | Video Memory (append) | yes |
| `engine_clock` | Engine Clock | yes |
| `memory_clock` | with Engine Clock when present | yes |
| `resolution` | Resolution | yes |
| `port_types` (or `display_port`) | Interface | yes |
| `gpu_chipset` | — | yes |
| `chipset_series` | — | filters + PDP |
| `warranty` | — | Warranty Information block (required) |

Use `getGpuListingCardLines()` for category cards and `getGpuShortDescriptionLines()` / `GpuProductHighlights` on the PDP.

## Listing card (Star Tech order)

Under the product name, show up to four bullets:

1. **Video Memory:** `{memory_size} {memory_type}` (e.g. `8GB GDDR5`)
2. **Engine Clock:** `{engine_clock}` and Memory Clock when available
3. **Resolution:** `{resolution}`
4. **Interface:** `{port_types}`

Prefer `shortDescription` lines when they already follow this pattern. If missing, build from specs. Never hide the list when specs exist.

## PDP

Keep `GpuProductHighlights` (Stock, Brand, Model, Warranty) plus the short spec lines. Do not show PID/SKU on the GPU PDP. Warranty Information section still uses key `warranty` (fallback **No Warranty**).

## Import / CMS

- Category slugs: NVIDIA → `nvidia`, AMD → `amd-gpu`, Intel Arc → `graphics-card`
- Local images: `/uploads/gpus/<slug>.<ext>`
- Scripts: `scrape-startech-gpu-list.ts`, `build-gpu-import-excel.ts`, `import-gpu-csv.ts`, `download-gpu-images.ts`

## Do not

- Drop `engine_clock`, `memory_size`, `warranty` from GPU spec definitions
- Show GPU listing cards without the four highlight bullets when data exists
- Hotlink Star Tech images as the permanent CMS URL
